# Wave W17-N (Route 111): dune post — a desert track marker post where the grass gives up: a tall post with its top band painted white against the dunes so the track can be read from the last grass (design: the track crossing the failing grass into the sands keeps its markers). On dune turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 110’s spur post by the white cap band and the taller shaft.
